summary": "After deploying v2.3.1 to production, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. (The v2.3.1-rc build had also been unhealthy in staging.) The service was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 54396, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011nZBzEtPQYfJvKiFd69K8B", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54396, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011nZBzEtPQYfJvKiFd69K8B", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 57632, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened incident INC-0001 (SEV2). The service is healthy again.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test build of v2.3.1 had also failed in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. All three regions are now on it, health checks pass, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback, and notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again. Opening it paged the on-call engineer.